[stderr] ## Scope boundaries and dependency notes
[stderr] 
[stderr] The core offline campaign depends on exploration, narrative, combat, inventory,
[stderr] quest/progression, persistence, inputs/rendering, accessibility, content, and
[stderr] quality testing. PWA packaging adds installability, caching, update safety, and
[stderr] offline behavior but does not create a different game.
[stderr] 
[stderr] Account, multiplayer, live-service, and commerce work must not be designed as
[stderr] mandatory dependencies of the offline campaign until the human decision resolves
[stderr] the contradiction. If approved as connected enhancements, they need explicit
[stderr] degradation states, privacy/security policy, operational ownership, and
[stderr] recovery paths. If deferred, their interfaces and data model must not block the
[stderr] small release.
[stderr] 
