[stderr] +an implementation commitment. Labels mean: **explicit** (directly requested),
[stderr] +**implied** (necessary to fulfill a direct request), **assumed** (safe temporary
[stderr] +guardrail), **deferred** (later scope), and **requires-decision** (not safely
[stderr] +selectable from the source).
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Candidate system map
[stderr] +
[stderr] +| Discipline / system family | Label | Rationale | Source reference |
[stderr] +| --- | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] +| Game shell, lifecycle, pause, navigation, and session recovery | implied | A playable web/PWA game needs safe entry, pause, resume, and return from interruption. | What are we creating?; selected targets |
[stderr] +| Exploration, traversal, collision, town and dungeon scenes | explicit | Exploration and exactly one town and one dungeon are named. | What are we creating? |
[stderr] +| Narrative, characters, dialogue, quest text, and short ending | explicit | Story/campaign progress, readable dialogue, quests, and a short ending are direct. | Users; shared requirements; creation scope |
[stderr] +| Quest state, progression, rewards, and onboarding/tutorial | explicit | Quests, progression, and onboarding are required; first session teaches battle and saving. | Required capabilities; first useful session |
[stderr] +| Party combat, encounters, turn resolution, rewards, and balancing | explicit | Turn-based combat is named; party scope comes only from the functional reference. Balancing is necessary for a learnable loop. | Creation scope; functional reference |
[stderr] +| Inventory, item definitions, equipment/use rules, and reward economy | explicit | Inventory is named and needs authored items/rewards. | Creation scope; shared UI requirements |
[stderr] +| Save/load, checkpoints, migrations, data-loss recovery, and local persistence | explicit | Save/load, long-session checkpoints, recovery, and offline PWA save behavior are direct. | Shared requirements; PWA requirements |
[stderr] +| Rendering, responsive layout, input adapter, and browser performance | explicit | Web target demands responsive layout, keyboard/mouse/touch/gamepad, compatibility, and performance budget. | Responsive web requirements |
[stderr] +| PWA installability, service worker, cache lifecycle, offline asset delivery, and update safety | explicit | Installability, offline assets/save behavior, and safe cache refresh are direct. | PWA requirements |
[stderr] +| Accessibility: remappable/accessible controls, text, captions, visual settings, and readable UI | explicit | Accessibility and readability are named across controls and core game interfaces. | Shared requirements |
[stderr] +| Localisation and language-content pipeline | explicit | Localisation is required, though languages are unknown. | Cross-platform decisions |
[stderr] +| Audio/visual feedback and original art asset pipeline | explicit | Feedback and original warm hand-painted direction are requested. | Required capabilities; art direction |
[stderr] +| Content authoring, validation, packaging, and level delivery | implied | Town, dungeon, dialogue, quests, items, and level delivery require controlled authored content and validation. | Content/level delivery; explicit scope |
[stderr] +| Build, release, versioning, cache/update communication, and rollback policy | implied | Safe web/PWA refresh cannot be delivered without release discipline. | PWA requirements |
[stderr] +| Crash diagnostics, error boundaries, player recovery UI, and support triage | explicit | Crash reporting and player-facing error recovery are direct. | Shared requirements; required capabilities |
[stderr] +| Quality engineering: gameplay, compatibility, offline/update, persistence/recovery, accessibility, and performance testing | implied | Every target and recovery promise needs validation beyond individual screens. | Per-target and shared requirements |
[stderr] +| Privacy, security, consent, data minimisation, retention/deletion | explicit | Privacy is required and accounts/diagnostics may process player data. | Constraints; cross-platform decisions |
[stderr] +| Account identity, authentication, remote state sync, and conflict handling | requires-decision | Named as required but no account/sync policy exists and it conflicts with offline scope. | Required capabilities; cross-platform data policy |
[stderr] +| Multiplayer, player safety, moderation/reporting, and community operations | requires-decision | Named as required but inconsistent with the single-player framing and lacks mode/safety policy. | Game characteristics; required capabilities |
[stderr] +| Live-service operations, status, support, incident response, and event tooling | requires-decision | Named as required but conflicts with a deliberately small offline release. | Required capabilities; creation scope |
[stderr] +| Purchases, catalogue, entitlements, refunds, and compliance | requires-decision | Named as required while monetisation is deferred and no payment/platform policy is given. | Required and deferred capabilities |
[stderr] +| Analytics and telemetry | deferred | Advanced analytics is explicitly later; minimum crash diagnostics remain separately required. | Later/deferred capabilities |
[stderr] +| Seasonal/live events and player-created/shared content | deferred | These are explicitly listed as later scope. | Later/deferred capabilities |
[stderr] +| Repository, engine/framework, backend/vendors, CI/CD, and cost model | requires-decision | The source says to determine constraints but authorizes no selection. | Constraints and non-goals |
[stderr] +| Browser/device matrix, storage quota, network floor, and performance budget | requires-decision | “Widely used” and “feasible slow-network” are not testable thresholds. | Cross-platform decisions; web requirements |
[stderr] +| Age rating, parental controls, regions, store/certification, and legal policy | requires-decision | Applicable requirements are named but audience detail, regions, and commerce/service scope are unknown. | Cross-platform decisions |
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Scope and dependency conclusions
[stderr] +
[stderr] +The minimal offline campaign depends on the shell, exploration, narrative,
[stderr] +quests/progression, combat, inventory, persistence, rendering/input,
[stderr] +accessibility, original assets, content tooling, and quality disciplines. PWA
[stderr] +packaging adds installability, caches, offline assets, and update safety; it
[stderr] +does not create a separate game.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Account, multiplayer, live-service, and commerce must not become dependencies
[stderr] +of the offline campaign until a human resolves their contradiction. If approved,
[stderr] +they require explicit degraded states, privacy/security rules, operational
[stderr] +ownership, and recovery behavior. If deferred, their interfaces and data model
[stderr] +must not expand or block the first release.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Explicit requests, safe assumptions, and approval gates
[stderr] +
[stderr] +| Kind | Discovery conclusion | Handling |
[stderr] +| --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] +| Explicit requests | Small 2D single-player RPG; web/PWA; exploration, town, dungeon, combat, inventory, quests, saves, settings, ending, access, feedback, recovery. | Plan as the complete offline campaign. |
[stderr] +| Necessary implied capabilities | Shell/session, authored content/tooling, input/rendering, QA, release/update workflow, and balance. | Include in later contracts as enabling work, sized to the small release. |
[stderr] +| Safe assumptions | Original content; shared core; durable confirmed local saves when storage permits; connected features visibly degrade; minimal-data diagnostics. | Retain as reversible guardrails only. |
[stderr] +| Approval gates | Connected scope, account/sync, multiplayer/safety, commerce, stack/vendors, support matrix/budgets, content quantities, localisation, audio, and legal/store policy. | Record and obtain approval before selecting policies, services, or production quantities. |
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Reference boundary
[stderr] +
[stderr] +The functional reference constrains high-level party-based turn-based adventure
[stderr] +scope only. It is never permission to reproduce branding, names, copy, story,
[stderr] +characters, lore, assets, music, layouts, screen composition, maps, distinctive
[stderr] +menus, flows, or interaction choreography. Original mechanics expression,
