[stderr] +## Scope and dependency conclusions
[stderr] +
[stderr] +The minimal offline campaign depends on the shell, exploration, narrative,
[stderr] +quests/progression, combat, inventory, persistence, rendering/input,
[stderr] +accessibility, original assets, content tooling, and quality disciplines. PWA
[stderr] +packaging adds installability, caches, offline assets, and update safety; it
[stderr] +does not create a separate game.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Account, multiplayer, live-service, and commerce must not become dependencies
[stderr] +of the offline campaign until a human resolves their contradiction. If approved,
[stderr] +they require explicit degraded states, privacy/security rules, operational
[stderr] +ownership, and recovery behavior. If deferred, their interfaces and data model
[stderr] +must not expand or block the first release.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Explicit requests, safe assumptions, and approval gates
